Methanol can be prepared synthetically by heating carbon monoxide and hydrogen gases under pressure in the presence of a catalyst.

\begin{aligned}
& $\mathrm{C} \text{ (graphite) }+$1 / 2 $\mathrm{O}_2$ \rightarrow $\mathrm{CO}_{(g)}$ \\
& $\mathrm{CO}_{(g)}+$2 $\mathrm{H}_{2(g)}$ \rightarrow $\mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{OH}$
\end{aligned}
$ \overline{\mathrm{C} \text{ (graphite) }+1 / 2 \mathrm{O}_{2(g)}+2 \mathrm{H}_{2(g)} \rightarrow \mathrm{CH}_3 \mathrm{OH}_{(l)}}$

